  "excluded": [
    "`from .models import *` and `from .shapes import *` import no single name, so their IMPORTS edge lands on the module itself (`py:app.models`, `py:app.shapes`) — the star binds names for callers, which is what the CALLS edges measure.",
    "`__all__ = [\"Order\"]` is a module-level constant — not modelled (see python/plain). It is read, not labelled: it is why `Draft` is not bound by the star import and why no edge reaches `Draft`.",
    "`app._private` is not bound by `from .shapes import *` (no `__all__`, leading underscore) and nothing calls it; it is labelled only as a node.",
    "No package->submodule CONTAINS: the graph does not model package nesting (see python/relative_imports)."
